    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "PROBLEM — why care",
      "role_note": "the stakes BEFORE the build begins — no terminal yet",
      "narration_text": "Two tables, same company, different strings. The visa filing says 'Acme, Inc.' The funding record says 'ACME Incorporated.' A naive join misses the match and the candidate looking at sponsorship history sees 'Unknown' — a false negative about a company that sponsors every year. That's not a minor data quality issue: it's a decision made wrong, made invisible, and repeated for every candidate who looked at the same table. String normalization closes the gap without a model, and fuzzy matching after that requires a human in the loop.",
      "visual_intent": "title card: 'same company, different string — the join miss that becomes a wrong decision'; PROBLEM beat, no terminal yet",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "same company, different string — the join miss that becomes a wrong decision",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM",
            "segment": "Entity-Resolution Matcher, taken apart.",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "framing the problem…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:21:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "ASK",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — the command typed",
      "narration_text": "In the terminal: ask Claude to write a normalize underscore employer function that lowercases, strips punctuation, and removes legal suffixes — inc, LLC, corp, ltd, co, incorporated, limited. Then join two fixture CSVs on the normalized name, print before and after join-coverage counts, the delta, and five rescued rows. Fuzzy matching is off by default: if the allow-fuzzy flag is passed, every proposed match prints as 'needs human confirmation' — it never auto-accepts.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"Write normalize_employer(name):\n  lowercase, strip punctuation, remove legal suffixes\n  (inc, llc, corp, ltd, co, incorporated, limited).\nJoin dol_sponsors.csv + sec_fundings.csv on\nnormalized name. Print:\n  rows matched before, after, delta, 5 rescued rows.\nNo auto-accept fuzzy — flag 'needs human confirmation'\nif --allow-fuzzy passed.\"",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM — VERIFIED DATA",
            "segment": "ENTITY-RESOLUTION MATCHER",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "generating entity-resolution module…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:21:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODE",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — read the output before running",
      "narration_text": "Read the normalization function before running. Three steps, in order: lowercase, strip punctuation with a regex substitution, remove legal suffixes with a second regex, collapse whitespace. The join key is the normalized name — not the original, not a hash, the readable normalized string so you can inspect every rescued row by eye. That inspectability is the contract: every rescued match has to be verifiable without trusting the algorithm.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "normalize_employer.py",
            "code": "# normalize_employer.py — Claude Code output\nimport re\n\nLEGAL_SUFFIXES = re.compile(\n    r\"\\b(inc|llc|corp|ltd|co|incorporated|limited)\\b\"\n)\n\ndef normalize_employer(name: str) -> str:\n    name = name.lower()\n    name = re.sub(r\"[^\\w\\s]\", \" \", name)   # strip punct\n    name = LEGAL_SUFFIXES.sub(\"\", name)      # drop suffixes\n    return \" \".join(name.split())            # collapse spaces\n\n# join on the readable normalized key\ndf_dol[\"key\"] = df_dol[\"employer\"].apply(normalize_employer)\ndf_sec[\"key\"] = df_sec[\"employer\"].apply(normalize_employer)\nmerged = df_dol.merge(df_sec, on=\"key\", how=\"inner\")",
            "sparkLine": "ENTITY-RESOLUTION MATCHER"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:21:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "OUTPUT — run",
      "role_note": "screen-recording — before/after coverage counts + rescued rows sample",
      "narration_text": "Run it on the fixtures. Before normalization: sixty-one matches. After: eighty-nine. Twenty-eight rescued rows — companies that appeared in both tables with identical legal substance and different formatting. The sample prints: 'Acme, Inc.' and 'ACME Incorporated' now share a key. No fuzzy matching, no embedding distance, no model — just case, punctuation, and three regex substitutions. Every rescued row is readable and verifiable by a human in under a second.",
      "visual_intent": "screen-recording: before/after counts printing (61 → 89, delta +28), 5 rescued rows showing exact string pairs that normalize to the same key",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "terminal: python normalize_employer.py",
            "code": "$ python normalize_employer.py\n\nBefore normalization: 61 matched rows\nAfter normalization:  89 matched rows\nDelta: +28 rescued rows\n\nSample rescued rows:\n  'Acme, Inc.'         → 'ACME Incorporated'\n  'Google LLC'         → 'Google, L.L.C.'\n  'Meta Platforms Inc' → 'Meta Platforms, Inc.'\n  'JPMorgan Chase & Co'→ 'JPMorgan Chase and Co.'\n  'Abbott Laboratories'→ 'Abbott Laboratories Ltd'",
            "sparkLine": "ENTITY-RESOLUTION MATCHER"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
